                  "displayName" : "Lewis Pringle",
                  "self" : "https://stroika.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4fe560ca-b4e1-41d1-9bdf-97b1684eda32",
                  "timeZone" : "America/New_York"
               },
               "body" : {
                  "content" : [
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "I THINK this is stragiht-forward and just requires crareful documentat.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "JUST change the = delete to = default for the ReadOnlyProperty constructors (and delete lots of code I had working around this).",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "BUT CAREFULLY DOCUMENT that the GETTERS must NEVER store the actual value, but rather COMPUTE it relative to the argument/given ‘this’ pointer pointing to that property in the callback function. I believe I always do that. It FORCES not BINDING the this - (maybe I did support that - but no longer can) - just always computing it from the argument.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     }
                  ],
                  "type" : "doc",
                  "version" : 1
               },
